A field $F$ on $\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^3$ with values in $\mathbb R^3$ is *$\Gamma$-invariant* if $$\begin{equation}
F(\theta+\theta_0,y)=R\,F(\theta,R^{-1}y)\qquad\text{for almost every }(\theta,y)\in\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^3\tag{7.5}
\end{equation}$$ and every $(R,\theta_0)\in\Gamma$, that is, if $F(\theta+\theta_0)=\rho_RF(\theta)$ for almost every $\theta$, with the action $\rho_R$ of (3.4).

